// noSwitch: Tanren rule, no `switch` statements (exhaustive Match instead).
//
// Pattern: every JsSwitchStatement, in any function, method or top level.
// `switch` is not exhaustive by construction: adding a union member compiles silently into
// `default` (or nothing). Match.exhaustive makes it a compile error.
//
// Fix: Match.value(x).pipe(Match.when(...), Match.exhaustive), Match.tag / Match.discriminators
// for tagged unions, or an `if` chain for two or three plain branches.
// Known gaps: none for `switch` statements. Ternary chains are not flagged.
//
// Suppress one line:  // biome-ignore lint/plugin/noSwitch: <reason>
// Verified with @biomejs/biome 2.5.15. Biome node names can change between releases.

JsSwitchStatement() as $switch where {
	register_diagnostic(
		span = $switch,
		message = "lint/plugin/noSwitch: `switch` is not allowed, use exhaustive Match (effect) instead of switch: Match.value(x).pipe(Match.when(...), Match.exhaustive).",
		severity = "error"
	)
}
